    #321 frame-ABI P0: add off-by-default +mos-dp-frame / +mos-sr-frame features + frameStrategy() plumbing
    
    P0 of the frame-ABI head-to-head study (docs/plans/2026-06-20-321-frame-abi-
    build-all-three-and-measure.md). Establish the selection plumbing so later
    phases (A1+ DP-window, B stack-relative) and the measurement harness can pick a
    frame strategy, WITHOUT touching the shipping soft-static path:
    
      - MOSFeatures.td: FeatureDPFrame (+mos-dp-frame), FeatureSRFrame (+mos-sr-frame),
        both OFF by default and NOT in any Family => default codegen unaffected.
      - MOSSubtarget.h: hasDPFrame()/hasSRFrame() getters, the HasDPFrame/HasSRFrame
        members, and a FrameStrategy {SoftStatic,DPWindow,StackRelative} tri-state
        frameStrategy() query (DP wins if both set; default SoftStatic).
    
    The branch-point switches (emitPrologue/emitEpilogue/eliminateFrameIndex) are
    DEFERRED to A1/B where they carry real logic — empty fall-through switches in
    hot functions are pure risk for zero functional value at this step.
    
    Captured in the worktree branch's 0002 (frame-abi delta merges to main's 0002
    only at GO; round-trips PASS, 22 files). New dev/frameabi-byte-identical.sh is
    the P0 guardrail.
    
    Verification (host-side, worktree toolchain rebuilt 06:40):
      - BYTE-IDENTICAL gate: corpus+kernels default + a16 disasm unchanged across the
        feature addition (24/24 entries identical).
      - +mos-dp-frame / +mos-sr-frame recognized (no unknown-feature warnings),
        present in generated MOSGenSubtargetInfo.inc, and INERT (output == default).
      - dev/run.sh corpus 7/7 still PASS.
    
